                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This Robin Hood adventure is not without charm. Ultimately, it's a platformer where you run and jump and climb around gathering treasure for your Band of Outlaws while defeating the Sheriff of Nottingham, his henchmen, and eventually the false king. You work your way through six levels, each with its own sort of unique boss. Personally, I found the boss battles to be very easy. You can almost just spam your bow attack and not worry about dodging. You will get their health down before they get yours down. A few of the better bosses feature the addition of a rush attack that you will dodge by jumping over the boss. Other than that, it's still all about spamming your attack button lol. The graphics are pretty nice overall and the audio is passable.\n\nDespite the design simplicity and relatively easy levels/bosses, I still thought this game was decent. Definitely a step above many of its bundle game contemporaries.\n\nI had zero technical issues btw, and my 360 gamepad worked fine.\n\nFor me, this is about a 5.5-6 out of 10. Worth keeping if you are buying stuff like Otaku bundles, and I appreciated a friend gifting it to me so I could give it a try. All told, you will complete this game in about 45 minutes, and although I didn't, you could probably 100% it on one run if you take your time.\n\n[code]If you found this review helpful and would be interested in supporting my Curator group, it would be appreciated. Cheers.\nhttps://store.steampowered.com/curator/32549618/[/code]",
